Go to make.powerautomate.com
Click "Create" on left sidebar
Click "Automated cloud flow"
Name it: Backlog to Gherkin Teams Flow


Step 2 — Set the Trigger

Search for trigger: "When a file is created" → choose OneDrive for Business
Set the folder to where you'll upload your Excel backlog

Example folder: /BDD Backlog


Click "New Step"


💡 Tip: Save your Excel backlog to OneDrive, not your local PC.


Step 3 — Read Excel Rows

Search action: "List rows present in a table" → choose Excel Online (Business)
Fill in:

Location: OneDrive for Business
Document Library: OneDrive
File: Select your Excel file
Table: Select your table name (your Excel must have a formatted Table — press Ctrl+T in Excel)


Click "New Step"


Step 4 — Loop Through Each Row

Search action: "Apply to each"
In the "Select an output" field, click and select "value" from the Excel step
Inside the loop, click "Add an action"


Step 5 — Call Your Copilot Studio Agent

Search action: "Microsoft Copilot Studio" → select "Ask a question" or "Generate text with agent"
Connect to your agent BDD Gherkin Generator
In the message/question field, type:

Generate Gherkin BDD scenarios for this test objective:
[click Dynamic Content → select your "Test Objective" column from Excel]

Click "New Step"


Step 6 — Post Result to Microsoft Teams

Search action: "Microsoft Teams" → select "Post a message in a chat or channel"
Fill in:

Post as: Flow bot
Post in: Channel
Team: Select your team
Channel: Select your channel (e.g., #bdd-scenarios)
Message:



🤖 New Gherkin Scenario Generated!

📋 Test Objective: [Dynamic Content → Test Objective column]

